// R-E / COMPILER — THE REFUSE HALF OF THE PAIR.
//
// The round-order fix (sema.cpp's typeof container arm; sema_expr.cpp's
// expect_type) makes a not-yet-produced type a DEMAND instead of a round-0
// error. That is permissive by shape, so it needs a program that must still be
// REFUSED — otherwise the relaxation is invisible to a green corpus (a
// permissive defect never reds a working program).
//
// THIS program names `<typeof(Fed) as CtrLeafFamily>::LeafWalk` as a STRUCT
// FIELD. Two independent reasons keep it refused, and the fixture pins the
// boundary, not the wording:
//
//   1. THE FAMILY IS NEVER DEMANDED. It is generated on demand and only a
//      VALUE use (`create_ctr::<typeof(Fed)>`) records that demand, so the
//      projection is unresolvable in EVERY round, not just the first. Measured:
//      probe p1 (this shape) refuses, p2 (identical plus a `create_ctr`)
//      compiles. Raising the demand from TYPE resolution was tried and made
//      every probe worse — "the factory did not satisfy the deferred trait
//      obligation … the CtrFamily impl is missing after the drain round".
//
//      REASON 1 IS NOW THE ONLY REASON. This fixture used to carry a second:
//      "the field position itself is not admitted yet", grounded on the
//      metaprog-round widening aborting under LOGOS_VERIFY_LAYOUT with
//      `[declined] <kind 32>`. #61 landed that widening together with the
//      layout half (declines and ledger answers carry the gen ROUND; the final
//      round's answer supersedes a metaprog snapshot's), and the field position
//      is admitted — pass/typeof_container_field_admit drives it and checks its
//      values. What keeps THIS program refused is reason 1 alone, and the
//      refusal is unchanged: `mlir_gen: unknown field type in 'NoFamilyState'`
//      from the FINAL gen, because no round can ever resolve a family nothing
//      demanded.
//
// So: `typeof(<container>)` is spellable, CALLABLE and now STORABLE in a
// hand-written item of the declaring module — as long as some value use
// demands the family. This fixture is the boundary: no demand, no type, and the
// compile is refused at the last gen rather than at the first.
package typeof_container_field_no_family_fail;

use logos.lcm.canon.container_item;
use logos.lcm.canon.metaclass;
use logos.mem.bt.map;
use logos.mem.bt.memstore;
use logos.mem.sync;
use logos.lang.stream;
use logos.lang.option;
use logos.mem.bt.batch;

pub container Fed {
    kind ordered_map;
    entry { key: u64, val: u64 }
    measure count;
    measure max(key);
}

pub struct NoFamilyState {
    w: <typeof(Fed) as CtrLeafFamily>::LeafWalk,
}

fn main() -> i32 { return 0i32; }
